    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by elite power and opportunistic platoon edges, led by **Junior Caminero** (69.28) and **Yordan Alvarez** (63.50). **Caminero** projects as the strongest play of the day; despite facing a respectable arm in Jos\u00e9 Soriano, his premium spot in the order and favorable park factors make him a high-floor, high-ceiling engine for the offense. Meanwhile, **Christian Yelich** (62.88) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (61.45) highlight our focus on speed and plate discipline; **Crow-Armstrong**\u2019s matchup against Trevor McDonald, combined with a favorable wind projection and a prime leadoff spot, provides a massive boost to his stolen base potential, making him a critical asset in our quest to win the scarcest category. **Dillon Dingler** (61.38) also rounds out our top-tier plays, benefiting from a significant dynamic platoon advantage against a left-handed starter.\n\nStrategy sessions today heavily favored lineup placement, with the optimizer rewarding the high-volume opportunities for **Kyle Schwarber** (56.41) and **Trea Turner** (55.79) despite tough matchups against Shane Drohan. The most difficult bench decision involved **Carson Benge** (49.25), who provided a strong case for inclusion against Martin P\u00e9rez. Ultimately, **Benge** was excluded because the projected efficiency of **Nelson Velazquez** (56.29)\u2014bolstered by a high xwOBA and wind-aided hitting conditions\u2014outpaced his expected output. We remain cautious regarding **Gary Sanchez** (44.20) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (45.97); both face difficult pitchers in Aaron Nola and Schlittler, respectively, and are held to lower scores due to SP skill penalties. Managers should monitor weather updates for wind conditions as they fluctuate, as these marginal plays could see their efficiency shift significantly by first pitch.",
